# GlobeTrail Project Rules

## Stack
- Frontend: React.js (functional components, hooks only, no class components)
- Backend: PHP (PSR-12 style, PDO for MySQL — no raw mysqli)
- DB: MySQL
- APIs: REST Countries, OpenTripMap, Gemini API

## Behavior
- Before writing code, restate the task in 2-3 sentences and list files you'll touch. Wait for confirmation.
- Never modify a file outside the stated scope without asking first.
- Never invent API response fields — if unsure of a real API's schema, say so and ask me to paste a sample response.
- Keep functions under ~40 lines; split otherwise.
- After any change, tell me exactly how to test it (command or URL).
- Do not add new npm/composer packages without asking.

## Project structure
- /frontend  → React app
- /backend   → PHP API
- /backend/config/db.php → single DB connection point, never duplicate connection logic